  "reasoning": "Based on the evidence, Matteo Renzi, the Prime Minister of Italy (a G7 member), officially visited Iran on 12 April 2016 [2][3]. This date falls before the target deadline of 1 July 2016. Prior to this date, no other G7 leader had visited Iran [1], but the occurrence of Renzi's visit confirms that at least one G7 head of government did host an official visit to Iran within the specified timeframe. The event is well-documented as a major diplomatic mission involving bilateral agreements and high-level meetings with President Rouhani [2][3].",
